Title: Cold Eggs
Credit: written by
Author: A. Previs

# Act One

INT. KITCHEN - DAY

Maya fries an egg at the counter. The radio mutters the shipping
forecast to nobody. Kai stumbles in, half asleep, and drops onto
a stool.

MAYA
You're late. The eggs are cold.

KAI
(yawning)
The eggs are always cold.

MAYA
Then maybe don't be late.

KAI
It's a system. It works.

[[ the radio should name the storm from scene two ]]

EXT. CLIFF PATH - DUSK

Wind. The lighthouse blinks out at sea. June waits by the gate,
collar up against the spray.

JUNE
You came.

MAYA
We argued about it.

KAI
I lost the argument.

JUNE
(pointing at the sea)
There. Where the gulls won't go.

>FADE OUT.
